Removing the blockquote brings the indented code block next to the list.
Blank lines do not end a list, and 4 spaces is enough to continue the last
item, so a plain splice would make the code a paragraph of that item. No
document can hold a top level indented code block directly below a list.

The code block is therefore written with a fence, which is the canonical
spelling of md and ends the list at column 0. The code itself is unchanged,
and the document still holds one list and one code block. Only the block
that would otherwise be lost is re-spelled: the list above it keeps its
asterisk bullets.
